WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.444 --> 00:00:04.527
(Arabber shouting)

00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:09.106
- Arabbers carry fresh vegetables
and fruits around the city

00:00:09.106 --> 00:00:10.856
in horse-drawn carts.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.327
My grandfather's been
doing it all his life.

00:00:13.327 --> 00:00:16.074
He 80-something years old now.

00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:17.906
I've been doing it all my life,

00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:22.073
and it's been around 50, maybe
a hundred years before me.

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:28.318
Here in Baltimore, you got markets around,

00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:31.113
but you gotta have a
vehicle to get to 'em.

00:00:31.113 --> 00:00:34.480
It's gonna cost 'em to get
there, cost 'em to get back.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.439
So it's beneficial to a lot of people

00:00:36.439 --> 00:00:38.944
for the Arabbers to be on the streets.

00:00:38.944 --> 00:00:40.944
- Y'all have a good one.

00:00:42.505 --> 00:00:44.367
Every morning, pull my wagon out,

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.591
I get all the fruit
together and design it up,

00:00:46.591 --> 00:00:48.103
make it look nice.

00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:50.383
And then I take the horse
and put him on the wagon

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.582
and I start on my day.

00:00:51.582 --> 00:00:52.566
(bells jingling)

00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:53.422
(Arabber shouting)

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:55.572
You mostly call out what
you got on your wagon.

00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:57.822
We have oranges and apples.

00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:02.008
- Peaches are awesome.

00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:04.344
- When you come out and
you see an elderly person

00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:06.625
just waiting at the door
for you to come through,

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:08.160
and they give you their little list.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.035
That's a wonderful feeling.

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:13.921
Well, they depend on us and
we try to be there for 'em.

00:01:13.921 --> 00:01:17.588
- Arabbers for life
baby, Arabbers for life.

00:01:20.315 --> 00:01:23.469
- The kids, they love the horses,

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:24.776
and I want them to be able to see

00:01:24.776 --> 00:01:28.943
that selling drugs ain't
the only way to make money.

00:01:30.206 --> 00:01:31.887
This is what keep me out of trouble,

00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:33.212
this is what feed my family,

00:01:33.212 --> 00:01:34.876
this is what put food on the table,

00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:36.929
pay the bills, pay the gas.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.065
This is one of the
oldest things in the city

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:41.409
that's still going right now.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:42.742
This is history.

00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:45.481
- When I was a little kid,

00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:46.929
it was nothing for me to turn a corner,

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:51.105
see an Arabber, one right
behind another sometimes.

00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:53.425
If we don't get a lot of people behind us,

00:01:53.425 --> 00:01:55.545
and expose the Arabbing business,

00:01:55.545 --> 00:01:58.089
it might eventually die out.

00:01:58.089 --> 00:02:00.500
But my dream is to see it last forever,

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.583
Till the day I shut my eyes for good.

